				if i == 0 || text[i-1] == ' ' || text[i-1] == '\t' || text[i-1] == '\n' || text[i-1] == ';' {
					push(tokComment, text[i:j])
					i = j
					continue
				}
			}
		}
		if (lang == langJS || lang == langGo) && c == '/' && i+1 < n && text[i+1] == '/' {
			j := i
			for j < n && text[j] != '\n' { j++ }
			push(tokComment, text[i:j])
			i = j
			continue
		}
		if (lang == langJS || lang == langGo || lang == langPython || lang == langBash || lang == langGeneric) && c == '/' && i+1 < n && text[i+1] == '*' {
			j := strings.Index(text[i+2:], "*/")
			end := n
			if j >= 0 { end = i + 2 + j + 2 }
			push(tokComment, text[i:end])
			i = end
			continue
		}
		// strings
		if c == '"' || c == '\'' || c == '`' {
			quote := c
			j := i + 1
			for j < n {
				if text[j] == '\\' && quote != '`' {
					j += 2
					continue
				}
				if text[j] == quote {
					j++
					break
				}
				if text[j] == '\n' && quote != '`' {
					break
				}
				j++
			}
			if j > n { j = n }
			push(tokString, text[i:j])
			i = j
			continue
		}
		// python triple strings
		if lang == langPython && (strings.HasPrefix(text[i:], "\"\"\"") || strings.HasPrefix(text[i:], "'''")) {
			q := text[i : i+3]
			j := strings.Index(text[i+3:], q)
			end := n
			if j >= 0 { end = i + 3 + j + 3 }
			push(tokString, text[i:end])
			i = end
			continue
		}
		// numbers
		if c >= '0' && c <= '9' {
			j := i
			for j < n && (isWordChar(text[j]) || text[j] == '.') { j++ }
			push(tokNumber, text[i:j])
			i = j
			continue
		}
		// words
		if isWordStart(c) {
			j := i
			for j < n && isWordChar(text[j]) { j++ }
			word := text[i:j]
			kw := false
			var kwmap map[string]bool
			switch lang {
			case langBash: kwmap = bashKeywords
			case langPython, langGeneric: kwmap = pythonKeywords
			case langJS: kwmap = jsKeywords
			case langGo: kwmap = goKeywords
			}
			if kwmap != nil && kwmap[word] { kw = true }
			// generic analysed lexer approximates python/js keywords union:
			if lang == langGeneric && (jsKeywords[word] || pythonKeywords[word] || bashKeywords[word]) { kw = true }
			if kw {
				push(tokKeyword, word)
				if word == "def" || word == "class" || word == "function" || word == "func" {
					nextIsFuncName = true
				}
			} else if nextIsFuncName {
				push(tokNameFunc, word)
				nextIsFuncName = false
			} else {
				if lang == langJS || lang == langGo {
					push(tokNameFunc, word) // names are green in these lexers under monokai
				} else {
					push(tokText, word)
				}
				nextIsFuncName = false
			}
			i = j
			continue
		}
		// whitespace - attach spaces to surrounding? chroma usually groups
		// a run of whitespace/text, but per-token escapes matter less if same colour.
		// We emit whitespace runs as text tokens.
		if c == ' ' || c == '\t' || c == '\r' {
			j := i
			for j < n && (text[j] == ' ' || text[j] == '\t' || text[j] == '\r') { j++ }
			push(tokText, text[i:j])
			i = j
			continue
		}
		// operators / punctuation single char grouping for some
		if strings.ContainsRune("=+-*/%<>!&|^~?:@$;,.()[]{}", rune(c)) {
			// In Go, = and punctuation are Text, not operator pink except some ops.
			if lang == langGo && strings.ContainsRune("=()[]{};,.", rune(c)) {
				push(tokText, string(c))
			} else if lang == langPython && strings.ContainsRune("()[]{}:;,.", rune(c)) {
				push(tokText, string(c))
			} else if lang == langJS && strings.ContainsRune("()[]{};,.", rune(c)) {
				// JS: () {} ; etc often Text, = + are operator pink? observed () was text, = pink, + pink, => text in JS (231) vs TS pink.
				push(tokText, string(c))
			} else if lang == langBash && strings.ContainsRune("()[]{};", rune(c)) {
				// bash parentheses pink in observed? () was pink (197)
				push(tokOperator, string(c))
			} else {
				push(tokOperator, string(c))
			}
			i++
			// reset func name flag on non-space token except? simplified
			if c != ' ' {
				// keep nextIsFuncName only over whitespace; punctuation clears
				if !(c == ' ') { nextIsFuncName = nextIsFuncName && false }
			}
			continue
		}
		// Error characters for Go/JS lexers: e.g. # in Go/JS
		if (lang == langJS || lang == langGo) && c == '#' {
			push(tokError, string(c))
			i++
			continue
		}
		// any other char
		push(tokText, text[i:i+1])
		i++
	}
	return toks
}

// ---- styles ----

func styleFor(name string, tokTyp int, lang langKind) styleEntry {
	// returns entry; zero fg (empty) means no colour (may still have italic)
	switch name {
	case "":
		// chroma styles.Get("") behaviour observed: comment italic, others plain
		if tokTyp == tokComment {
			return styleEntry{italic: true}
		}
		return styleEntry{}
	case "monokai":
		switch tokTyp {
		case tokComment: return styleEntry{fg: "75715e"}
		case tokKeyword: return styleEntry{fg: "66d9ef"}
		case tokOperator: return styleEntry{fg: "f92672"}
		case tokNumber: return styleEntry{fg: "ae81ff"}
		case tokString: return styleEntry{fg: "e6db74"}
		case tokNameFunc: return styleEntry{fg: "a6e22e"}
		case tokError: fg89 := 89; bg232 := 232; return styleEntry{fg: "f92672", bg: "272822", fg256: &fg89, bg256: &bg232}
		default: return styleEntry{fg: "f8f8f2"}
		}
	case "github":
		switch tokTyp {
		case tokComment: return styleEntry{fg: "57606a"}
		case tokKeyword: return styleEntry{fg: "cf222e"}
		case tokOperator: return styleEntry{fg: "0550ae"}
		case tokNumber: return styleEntry{fg: "0550ae"}
		case tokString: return styleEntry{fg: "0a3069"}
		case tokNameFunc: return styleEntry{fg: "1f2328"}
		case tokError: return styleEntry{fg: "cf222e"}
		default: return styleEntry{fg: "1f2328"}
		}
	case "dracula":
		switch tokTyp {
		case tokComment: return styleEntry{fg: "6272a4"}
		case tokKeyword: return styleEntry{fg: "ff79c6"}
		case tokOperator: return styleEntry{fg: "ff79c6"}
		case tokNumber: return styleEntry{fg: "bd93f9"}
		case tokString: return styleEntry{fg: "f1fa8c"}
		case tokNameFunc: return styleEntry{fg: "50fa7b"}
		default: return styleEntry{fg: "f8f8f2"}
		}
	default:
		// fallback / swapoff style used by chroma for unknown styles
		switch tokTyp {
		case tokComment: return styleEntry{fg: "00ffff"} // approx 256 -> 6
		case tokKeyword: return styleEntry{fg: "00ffff"}
		case tokOperator: return styleEntry{fg: "00ffff"}
		case tokNumber: return styleEntry{fg: "ff00ff"}
		case tokString: return styleEntry{fg: "ffff00"}
		case tokNameFunc: return styleEntry{fg: "00ff00"}
		default:
			// swapoff text ~ e4e4e4 -> 254
			fg := 254; return styleEntry{fg: "e4e4e4", fg256: &fg}
		}
	}
}

func hexToRGB(hex string) (int, int, int) {
	if len(hex) == 3 {
		hex = string([]byte{hex[0], hex[0], hex[1], hex[1], hex[2], hex[2]})
	}
	var v int
	fmt.Sscanf(hex, "%x", &v)
	return (v >> 16) & 255, (v >> 8) & 255, v & 255
}

func rgbTo256(r, g, b int) int {
	// approximate xterm 256 conversion like chroma
	if r == g && g == b {
		if r < 8 { return 16 }
		if r > 248 { return 231 }
		return int(math.Round(float64(r-8)/247*24)) + 232
	}
	to6 := func(c int) int {
		if c < 48 { return 0 }
		if c < 115 { return 1 }
		return int(math.Round(float64(c-55)/40.0))
		// note chroma uses a colour distance palette; this approximates
	}
	// Use chroma-like nearest cube/grey selection via palette distance
	best := 16
	bestDist := math.MaxFloat64
	// build xterm palette
	type rgb struct{ r, g, b int }
	var pal []rgb
	base := []rgb{{0,0,0},{128,0,0},{0,128,0},{128,128,0},{0,0,128},{128,0,128},{0,128,128},{192,192,192},{128,128,128},{255,0,0},{0,255,0},{255,255,0},{0,0,255},{255,0,255},{0,255,255},{255,255,255}}
	pal = append(pal, base...)
	levels := []int{0, 95, 135, 175, 215, 255}
	for _, rr := range levels {
		for _, gg := range levels {
			for _, bb := range levels {
				pal = append(pal, rgb{rr, gg, bb})
			}
		}
	}
	for i := 0; i < 24; i++ {
		v := 8 + i*10
		pal = append(pal, rgb{v, v, v})
	}
	_ = to6
	for idx, c := range pal {
		d := math.Sqrt(float64((r-c.r)*(r-c.r) + (g-c.g)*(g-c.g) + (b-c.b)*(b-c.b)))
		if d < bestDist {
			bestDist = d
			best = idx
		}
	}
	return best
}

func rgbToANSI16(r, g, b int) (int, bool) {
	type rgb struct{ r, g, b int }
	pal := []rgb{{0,0,0},{128,0,0},{0,128,0},{128,128,0},{0,0,128},{128,0,128},{0,128,128},{192,192,192},{128,128,128},{255,0,0},{0,255,0},{255,255,0},{0,0,255},{255,0,255},{0,255,255},{255,255,255}}
	best := 0
	bestDist := math.MaxFloat64
	for idx, c := range pal {
		d := float64((r-c.r)*(r-c.r) + (g-c.g)*(g-c.g) + (b-c.b)*(b-c.b))
		if d < bestDist { bestDist = d; best = idx }
	}
	code := 30 + (best % 8)
	bright := best >= 8
	return code, bright
}

func formatColored(text string, syntax string, cfg *config) string {
	if text == "" {
		return ""
	}
	lang := lexerForSyntax(syntax, text)
	toks := tokenize(text, lang)
	formatter := cfg.Formatter
	styleName := cfg.Style
	var sb strings.Builder
	writeToken := func(tok token) {
		if tok.val == "" {
			// mirrors occasional empty-token output when token is "\n" handled outside
			return
		}
		// split by newline: newline written outside styles
		parts := strings.Split(tok.val, "\n")
		for pi, part := range parts {
			if pi > 0 {
				sb.WriteString("\n")
			}
			if part == "" {
				// If token was exactly "\n", original formatter emits an empty
				// styled text token for some lexers. We approximate: a pure
				// newline token becomes newline only (no empty sequence) except
				// when caller inserts it specially.
				if tok.val == "\n" && pi == 0 {
					// newline already handled by caller logic below
				}
				continue
			}
			entry := styleFor(styleName, tok.typ, lang)
			seq := escapeSequence(entry, formatter)
			if seq == "" {
				sb.WriteString(part)
			} else {
				sb.WriteString(seq)
				sb.WriteString(part)
				sb.WriteString("\x1b[0m")
			}
		}
		// trailing newline of token: Split already inserted newlines between parts,
		// but if token ends with newline and part last empty we need newline.
		if strings.HasSuffix(tok.val, "\n") {
			// The loop wrote newlines between, and final empty skipped; ensure trailing
			// newline count is preserved:
			// Count trailing newlines:
			// Simpler: split logic above lost final newline. Add it if not already.
			// Our tokens: newline tokens are separate (tokText "\n") except strings etc.
			// For those, add newline now.
			if tok.typ == tokString || tok.typ == tokComment {
				sb.WriteString("\n")
			}
		}
	}
	for _, tok := range toks {
		if tok.val == "\n" {
			sb.WriteString("\n")
			continue
		}
		writeToken(tok)
	}
	return sb.String()
}

func escapeSequence(e styleEntry, formatter string) string {
	if e.fg == "" && e.bg == "" && !e.bold && !e.italic {
		return ""
	}
	switch formatter {
	case "terminal":
		var parts []string
		bright := false
		code := 0
		if e.fg != "" {
			r, g, b := hexToRGB(e.fg)
			code, bright = rgbToANSI16(r, g, b)
		}
		if bright || e.bold {
			parts = append(parts, "\x1b[1m")
		}
		if e.italic {
			parts = append(parts, "\x1b[3m")
		}
		if e.fg != "" {
			parts = append(parts, fmt.Sprintf("\x1b[%dm", code))
		}
		return strings.Join(parts, "")
	case "terminal16m":
		var sb strings.Builder
		if e.bold { sb.WriteString("\x1b[1m") }
		if e.italic { sb.WriteString("\x1b[3m") }
		// chroma terminal16m merges? Observed only fg sequence for monokai (no bold separate)
		// For entries with colours, return single 38;2 sequence (plus separate if attrs)
		var main strings.Builder
		if e.bold || e.italic {
			main.WriteString(sb.String())
		}
		if e.fg != "" {
			r, g, b := hexToRGB(e.fg)
			main.WriteString(fmt.Sprintf("\x1b[38;2;%d;%d;%dm", r, g, b))
		}
		if e.bg != "" {
			r, g, b := hexToRGB(e.bg)
			main.WriteString(fmt.Sprintf("\x1b[48;2;%d;%d;%dm", r, g, b))
		}
		return main.String()
	default: // terminal256 and "" fallback to terminal? Original: formatter "" + monokai gave terminal (16 colors)
		if formatter == "" {
			// chroma formatters.Get("") returns terminal fallback
			return escapeSequence(e, "terminal")
		}
		var sb strings.Builder
		if e.bold { sb.WriteString("\x1b[1m") }
		if e.italic { sb.WriteString("\x1b[3m") }
		if e.fg != "" {
			fg256 := 0
			if e.fg256 != nil {
				fg256 = *e.fg256
			} else {
				r, g, b := hexToRGB(e.fg)
				fg256 = rgbTo256(r, g, b)
			}
			sb.WriteString(fmt.Sprintf("\x1b[38;5;%dm", fg256))
		}
		if e.bg != "" {
			bg256 := 0
			if e.bg256 != nil {
				bg256 = *e.bg256
			} else {
				r, g, b := hexToRGB(e.bg)
				bg256 = rgbTo256(r, g, b)
			}
			sb.WriteString(fmt.Sprintf("\x1b[48;5;%dm", bg256))
		}
		return sb.String()
	}
}
GO"}

